Normal | [image 9525x9525]
Title | Rotate an API key
Subtitle | Replace a leaked or expiring API key without downtime.
Normal | Rotate keys every *90 days*, or right away if one leaks.
Heading1 | Prerequisites
Normal | Admin access to the console.
Normal shd=FFF4E5 | **Warning: **Creating a new key **revokes** the old one immediately. Update these first:
Normal num=2/0 shd=FFF4E5 | The CI secret
Normal num=2/0 shd=FFF4E5 | Local `.env` files
Heading2 | {#step-1}1. Open **Settings → API keys**
Normal | [image 304800x190500]
Heading2 | {#step-2}2. Enter your password to confirm
Normal | [image 609600x381000]
Normal | Password input is masked while recording.
Heading2 | {#step-3}3. Click **Create key** and copy the new key
Normal | [image 609600x190500]
Normal | The key is shown **once**. Store it in your password manager; see [Managing keys](https://example.com/docs/keys).
Normal shd=E8F0FE | **Decision: **Is the key used in **production**?
Normal shd=E8F0FE | –**Yes: **[Go to Step 4](#step-4)
Normal shd=E8F0FE | –**No: **[Go to Step 5](#step-5)
Normal shd=E8F0FE | –**Unsure: **Go to the guide “Find where an API key is used”
Heading2 | {#step-4}4. Drag the new key to **Production**
Normal | [image 609600x381000]
Heading2 | {#step-5}5. Check that the key works
Normal | [image 609600x381000]
Normal | Run this in Terminal:
Normal | `curl -H "x-api-key: $KEY" https://api.example.com/v1/ping`
Normal | It should print *pong*.
